# PROBE disjoint-nary. AllDisjointClasses(B C D) with A ⊑ B and A ⊑ D makes A unsatisfiable; E ⊑ B alone does not.
# construct: DisjointClasses
# expect: unsat :A
# expect-not: unsat :E

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class . :E a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf :B , :D .
:E rdfs:subClassOf :B .
[] a owl:AllDisjointClasses ; owl:members ( :B :C :D ) .
